# =============================================================================
# .npm-audit-ignore — Temporary exact npm-audit suppressions
# =============================================================================
#
# Read by .github/scripts/check_npm_audit.py. npm has no native advisory
# ignore-file support, so the checker compares each finding of MODERATE
# severity or above with every field below and fails closed when any field
# differs.
#
# Rules:
#   1. Scope every entry to one package graph, package, advisory, and node path.
#   2. Every entry MUST carry an expiration date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD). The listed
#      date is expired; there is no grace day.
#   3. Document the risk decision and link upstream tracking immediately above
#      the entry.
#   4. Remove an entry as soon as the dependency graph no longer reports it.
#      The checker rejects stale as well as expired suppressions.
#   5. Do not add entries for the "depends on vulnerable versions of X"
#      records npm derives when X has no fixed version in range. They carry
#      no advisory of their own; the checker accepts them once every package
#      they reach through is suppressed, and names each one in the job log.
#
# Format (exactly five pipe-delimited fields):
#   package-dir|package|advisory|node-path|exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# =============================================================================

# GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p (CVE-2026-102276, high), GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7
# (CVE-2026-102278, high) and GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr (CVE-2026-102277, moderate):
# three brace-expansion denial-of-service advisories published 2026-09-29.
# Two exhaust the stack through recursion (in parseCommaParts() and on nested
# brace groups); the third makes `{a},b}`-shaped input expand in quadratic
# time. On the 5.x line they are fixed in 5.0.10, 5.0.11 and 5.0.12.
#
# The one reported copy is brace-expansion 5.0.9, which aws-cdk-lib bundles
# (minimatch 10.2.5 -> brace-expansion) inside its published tarball. The root
# graph reaches aws-cdk-lib only through cdk-dia, the infrastructure diagram
# generator. A bundled copy is out of reach of `npm audit fix` and `overrides`,
# and Dependabot's security update fails on it for the same reason.
#
# Not clearable by a pin bump: checked 2026-09-30, aws-cdk-lib 2.271.0 (the
# latest release) still bundles brace-expansion 5.0.9. The upstream fix is
# https://github.com/aws/aws-cdk/pull/38929.
#
# Low risk: cdk-dia's runtime code never loads aws-cdk-lib. It matches the
# construct names in the synthesized cdk.out/tree.json as strings, and its only
# import of the library is a TypeScript type declaration. Diagram generation is
# contributor/CI tooling that never runs in a deployed service, and the impact
# of all three advisories is availability only.
#
# Remove these entries and refresh package-lock.json as soon as an aws-cdk-lib
# release bundles brace-expansion >= 5.0.12.
# Advisories: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p
#             https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7
#             https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr
.|brace-expansion|GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p|node_modules/aws-cdk-lib/node_modules/brace-expansion|exp:2026-10-30
.|brace-expansion|GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr|node_modules/aws-cdk-lib/node_modules/brace-expansion|exp:2026-10-30
.|brace-expansion|GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7|node_modules/aws-cdk-lib/node_modules/brace-expansion|exp:2026-10-30

# GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (CVE-2026-93687, high): braces, the brace-expansion
# engine behind micromatch, walks a pattern's nested brace groups recursively
# with no depth limit, so a deeply nested pattern exhausts the stack. Published
# 2026-09-18 against every release (<= 3.0.3).
#
# The one reported copy is braces 3.0.3 at node_modules/braces, reached only
# through markdownlint-cli2 0.23.3 -> globby 16.2.4 -> fast-glob 3.3.3 ->
# micromatch 4.0.8 -> braces ^3.0.3. markdownlint-cli2 is the Markdown linter
# the root graph installs for CI, pre-commit and `npm run lint:markdown`; no
# other owned graph depends on it.
#
# Not clearable by a pin bump: checked 2026-10-03, 3.0.3 (2024-09-18) is still
# the newest braces release, the advisory lists no patched version, and
# micromatch 4.0.8 is the newest micromatch, so every dependent up to
# markdownlint-cli2 is reported as "depends on vulnerable versions" (npm's only
# fix is downgrading markdownlint-cli2 to 0.0.4). The upstream report is
# https://github.com/micromatch/braces/issues/70.
#
# Low risk: the only patterns braces expands here are the `globs` and
# `ignores` in .github/config/.markdownlint-cli2.yaml and the file arguments
# the lint job and pre-commit hook pass, all authored in this repository. The
# linter is contributor/CI tooling that never runs in a deployed service, and
# the impact is availability only.
#
# Remove this entry and refresh package-lock.json as soon as braces publishes
# a release the advisory lists as patched (`npm update braces` picks it up
# through micromatch's ^3.0.3 range).
# Advisory: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm
.|braces|GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm|node_modules/braces|exp:2026-10-30
